{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794667082,"nonce":"+fLqO47PnMqFabQgD59MpILKxCo=","title":"Text is soft while a scale animation plays, though sharp once it settles","message":"A labelled card scaled from 1x to 2x by a CSS keyframe animation (300 ms, linear), headless Vector path, sharpness measured as in the animation_paths tests (gradient energy of the pixels the label adds over their energy), against the same label laid out natively at the scale the animation has reached. The scale is estimated from the frame's time, so the ratios are approximate.\n\nPlays: frame 4 (about 1.2x) 0.65, frame 8 (about 1.4x) 0.74, frame 12 (about 1.6x) 0.83. A label under a fade measures the same within 0.03.\nSettled at 2x: 1.00 unfaded, 1.04 faded.\n\nWhile an animation of the scale plays the glyphs are rasterized at the scale rounded up to a quarter and placed smoothly, not on whole device pixels, so each frame minifies a bitmap and resamples it at a fractional offset. At rest they are exact and on the grid.\n\nOptions to weigh: rasterize at the exact scale in flight (a new glyph size every frame, so atlas churn and a raster per frame), a finer step than a quarter, or snapping origins in flight (the text then steps by pixels while the card scales smoothly).\n\nRelated: 23b08b1b and 1e213504 made the settled case sharp. The grouped case (a card that fades as well) was 0.59 settled and is fixed with the work on d20f077.","files":null}]}